# The licence texts are asserted byte-for-byte by the chart contract test
# (charts/nilchela/tests/chart_contract.py, check_licenses): it pins the sha256
# of the root files and compares the chart-local copies against them. On a
# Windows checkout, text normalisation would rewrite those bytes and both checks
# would fail for a non-reason -- and the packaged chart would carry the rewritten
# text. `text eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF on every platform and keeps the
# files diffable, which `-text` would not.
#
# Unanchored patterns match at every directory level, so these three lines cover
# both the root copies and charts/nilchela/.
LICENSE-MIT text eol=lf
LICENSE-APACHE text eol=lf
NOTICE text eol=lf
